          "author": "Institute for Saharan Margins",
          "summary": "The Fezzan in insurgency since January 2026: what the 12 July attack on Al-Wigh reveals about the limits of Libyan National Army control, why the UN Panel of Experts report places the Chad-Libya joint force in direct contact with the Rapid Support Forces' supply chain, and how that same force carried the war up to 130 kilometres inside Niger.",
          "excerpt": "Since January 2026, the Operations Chamber for the Liberation of the South has contested LAAF control over the Fezzan. The UN Panel of Experts report on Libya establishes that the Subul Al-Salam battalion supplies the RSF in Sudan — the same battalion to which Saddam Haftar assigned operations of the joint force with the Chadian army.",
